# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Archives -- never commit these. A 57.9 MB DUNCS.7z was committed in 5824204 and deleted
# again later, but git keeps every version ever committed, so .git still carries it and is
# 275 MB as a result. Removing the file a second time reclaims nothing; only rewriting those
# commits would, and that was declined. These rules stop it happening again.
*.7z
*.zip
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
